IMPORT prelude

-- Dividing Fences Act 1961 (Western Australia) -- who pays for a dividing fence: the equal share of a new sufficient
-- fence (s 7), the notice to fence (ss 8, 22), going to the Magistrates Court (s 9), building the whole fence when the
-- other owner defaults (s 10), claiming half for a fence built without notice (s 13), the equal share of repairs, the
-- repair notice, urgent repairs and damage caused by one owner (ss 14, 15), landlord and tenant (s 19), entry (s 21),
-- and what counts as a sufficient fence as far as the Act states (s 5).
--
-- SEAT: the neighbouring owner -- one of the two owners of adjoining lands, either the one who wants a fence built or
-- repaired or the one asked to pay. Every decision is phrased as that owner would ask it: "Am I an owner under the Act",
-- "Is our fence a sufficient fence", "What share of a new dividing fence must I bear", "May I apply to the Magistrates
-- Court", "What can I recover for repairing the fence".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 4 (as an input: the Crown is not bound), s 5 (court, dividing fence, owner (a) and (b) and the
-- public-reserve exclusion, sufficient fence (a)-(d)), s 6(1), s 7, s 8, s 9(1) (the 21 days and who may apply), s 10,
-- s 13(1), (2), (3), (4), (7), s 14, s 15(1)-(4), (7)(a)-(c), (8), s 19(1), s 21, s 22(1), (2).
--
-- Edition: the compilation incorporating amendments up to the Community Titles Act 2018 (No. 32 of 2018, Pt 14 Div 5,
-- in operation 30 June 2021), last reprint listed Reprint 3 as at 22 May 2015, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_43948.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026). No regulations are used: the Act's own
-- numbers (21 days, 3 months, 14 days, one month, 5 years, the s 19 bands) are in the text. What a LOCAL LAW prescribes
-- as a sufficient fence (s 5(a), s 24) is not deposited and is an input.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 5(2) and s 6(2) (community titles schemes: the bylaws decide), s 9(1)(g), (h), (2), (3) (what the court
-- may order and is guided by: the court's judgment), s 11 (an owner who cannot be found), s 12 (defining the boundary by
-- surveyor), s 13(5), (6) and s 15(5)-(6) (the court's orders), s 16 (a road-boundary fence used by another owner),
-- s 17 (costs), s 18 (recovery), s 19(2), s 20 (purchaser under an option), s 22(3), (4). Machinery out: ss 1-3, 23, 24.
-- Lands that are not adjoining, or that are owned by the Crown (s 4), are answered "nothing under s 7".
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dividing Fences Act 1961 -- the neighbouring owner's questions`

§§ `s 5 -- am I an owner`

-- s 5(1): "owner, in relation to land, includes ... every person who -- (a) jointly or severally, whether at law or in
-- equity -- (i) is entitled to land for any estate of freehold in possession; or (ii) is entitled to receive or is in
-- receipt of ... the rents and profits of the land, whether as beneficial owner, trustee, mortgagee in possession, or
-- otherwise; or (b) is the holder of a lease of land the unexpired term of which is not less than 5 years at the time
-- -- (i) notice to fence is given by or to him pursuant to section 8; ... (iv) notice is given by or to him pursuant to
-- section 15, but does not include any trustees or other persons in whom land is vested as a public reserve, public park
-- or for such other public purposes as may be prescribed".
DECLARE `My interest in the land` IS ONE OF
    `I hold the freehold in possession`                                         -- s 5 owner (a)(i): the registered owner living on or holding the land
    `I am entitled to the rents and profits, for example as trustee or mortgagee in possession`  -- s 5 owner (a)(ii)
    `I hold a lease`                                                            -- s 5 owner (b), if 5 or more years are left
    `I only occupy the land`                                                    -- a licensee or lodger: no estate, no lease

@export Am I an owner of the land for the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5?
GIVEN `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What interest you have in the land
      `years left on my lease` IS A NUMBER @desc If you hold a lease: the unexpired term in years when the fencing or repair notice is given (0 otherwise)
      `the land is vested in me as a public reserve or park` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the land as trustee of a public reserve, public park or other prescribed public purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an owner under the Act` IF
        (NOT `the land is vested in me as a public reserve or park`)
    AND CONSIDER `my interest`
        WHEN `I hold the freehold in possession` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `I am entitled to the rents and profits, for example as trustee or mortgagee in possession` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `I hold a lease` THEN `years left on my lease` AT LEAST 5
        WHEN `I only occupy the land` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 5 -- what is a sufficient fence`

-- s 5(1): "sufficient fence ... means -- (a) any fence prescribed by a local law as a sufficient fence for the part of
-- the local government district in which the dividing fence ... is, or is to be, erected; or (b) any fence of the
-- description and quality agreed upon by the parties concerned which does not fail to comply with any local law referred
-- to in paragraph (a), or where no such local law or agreement is made, means -- (c) any substantial fence that is
-- ordinarily capable of resisting the trespass of cattle and sheep; or (d) any fence determined to be a sufficient fence
-- by the court pursuant to this Act".
-- Read literally, limbs (c) and (d) apply only "where no such local law or agreement is made". The encoding follows the
-- words: where a local law or an agreement exists, only (a) and (b) can make a fence sufficient. The court (the
-- Magistrates Court, s 5) is told by s 9(3) to be guided by the local law when it orders a fence, so the two rarely part.
@export Is our dividing fence a sufficient fence under the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5?
GIVEN `a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government's local law prescribes a sufficient fence for the part of the district where the fence is or will be
      `the fence is of a kind the local law prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is one the local law prescribes as sufficient
      `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agreed on the description and quality of the fence
      `the fence is of the kind we agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence matches what you agreed
      `the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law (FALSE if there is no local law)
      `the fence is substantial and ordinarily resists cattle and sheep` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is substantial and ordinarily capable of resisting the trespass of cattle and sheep
      `the court has determined it sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Magistrates Court has determined it to be a sufficient fence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the fence a sufficient fence` IF
        (`a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area` AND `the fence is of a kind the local law prescribes`)
    OR  (    `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality`
         AND `the fence is of the kind we agreed`
         AND (NOT `the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law`))
    OR  (    (NOT `a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area`)
         AND (NOT `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality`)
         AND (`the fence is substantial and ordinarily resists cattle and sheep` OR `the court has determined it sufficient`))

§§ `ss 4, 6, 7 -- my share of a new fence`

-- s 7: "Subject to this Act the owners of adjoining lands not divided by a sufficient fence are liable to join in or
-- contribute in equal proportions to the construction of a dividing fence between those lands."
-- s 6(1): "Nothing in this Act affects any covenant, contract or agreement made ... between the owners of adjoining lands
-- ... relative to the cost of erecting or repairing dividing fences."
-- s 4: "This Act does not bind the Crown."
DECLARE `My share of a new fence` IS ONE OF
    `half: we join in or contribute in equal proportions (s 7)`
    `as our agreement says: the Act does not affect it (s 6(1))`
    `nothing under s 7: our lands are already divided by a sufficient fence`
    `nothing under s 7: our lands do not adjoin`
    `nothing under s 7: I am not an owner as the Act defines it`
    `nothing under s 7: my neighbour is not an owner bound by the Act`

@export What share of a new dividing fence must I bear (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 4, 6, 7)?
GIVEN `I am an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner under s 5 (freehold, entitled to the rents, or a lease with 5 or more years left)
      `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour is an owner under s 5 and not the Crown (s 4)
      `our lands adjoin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land and your neighbour's land adjoin
      `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sufficient fence (s 5) already divides the two lands
      `we have an agreement about the cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour have a covenant, contract or agreement about the cost of the fence
GIVETH A `My share of a new fence`
DECIDE `What share of a new dividing fence must I bear` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I am an owner` THEN `nothing under s 7: I am not an owner as the Act defines it`
        IF NOT `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` THEN `nothing under s 7: my neighbour is not an owner bound by the Act`
        IF NOT `our lands adjoin` THEN `nothing under s 7: our lands do not adjoin`
        IF `we have an agreement about the cost` THEN `as our agreement says: the Act does not affect it (s 6(1))`
        IF `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` THEN `nothing under s 7: our lands are already divided by a sufficient fence`
        OTHERWISE `half: we join in or contribute in equal proportions (s 7)`

@export How much must I contribute to a new dividing fence under s 7, where there is no agreement about the cost?
GIVEN `the cost of the fence` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of constructing the dividing fence, in dollars
      `I am an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner under s 5
      `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour is an owner under s 5 and not the Crown
      `our lands adjoin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the two lands adjoin
      `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sufficient fence already divides the two lands
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute to the new fence` IS
    IF  `What share of a new dividing fence must I bear` `I am an owner` `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` `our lands adjoin` `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` FALSE
        EQUALS `half: we join in or contribute in equal proportions (s 7)`
    THEN `the cost of the fence` DIVIDED BY 2
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 8, 22 -- the notice I must give to make my neighbour contribute`

-- s 8: "An owner of land desiring to compel the owner of adjoining land to join in or contribute to the construction of
-- a dividing fence under this Act may give him a notice which shall -- (a) specify the boundary to be fenced, or if ...
-- it is impracticable to construct a fence on the common boundary ..., the line upon which it is proposed to construct
-- the fence; and (b) contain a proposal for fencing the common boundary or other line; and (c) specify the kind of fence
-- proposed to be constructed."
-- s 22(1): "Any notice or demand ... shall be in writing and signed by the person giving or making it, or by his attorney
-- or agent." (2): to a person not a corporation, "(a) by delivering ... to him personally; or (b) by sending ... by
-- registered mail addressed to him at his usual or last known place of abode". (3): to a corporation, at or to its
-- principal office in the State.
@export Is my notice to fence a valid notice under the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 8 and 22?
GIVEN `it is in writing and signed by me or my attorney or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is written and signed by you or your attorney or agent
      `it specifies the boundary, or the other line where the boundary is impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it names the boundary to be fenced (or another line, if the land makes the boundary impracticable)
      `it contains a proposal for fencing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains a proposal for fencing that boundary or line
      `it specifies the kind of fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the kind of fence proposed
      `it was delivered personally or sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was handed to your neighbour personally or sent by registered mail to their usual or last known home (for a company: left at or posted to its principal office in WA)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice to fence valid` IF
        `it is in writing and signed by me or my attorney or agent`
    AND `it specifies the boundary, or the other line where the boundary is impracticable`
    AND `it contains a proposal for fencing`
    AND `it specifies the kind of fence`
    AND `it was delivered personally or sent by registered mail`

§§ `s 9 -- when the dispute goes to the Magistrates Court`

-- s 9(1): "If within 21 days after the giving of a notice referred to in section 8, the owner giving and the owner
-- receiving the notice do not agree as to ... (a) ... the need for the construction of the dividing fence; or (b) the
-- boundary or line ...; or (c) the kind of dividing fence that is to be constructed, the court at the place nearest to
-- the place where it is proposed to erect the fence, on an application by either of those owners may make an order".
-- (4): "An order of the court made under this section is final."
-- Either owner may apply -- the one who gave the notice or the one who received it. The application lies once the 21
-- days have run without agreement; the encoding reads "after 21 days" as more than 21 days since the notice was given
-- (encoder's reading).
@export May I apply to the Magistrates Court to settle the new dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `a notice to fence was given by me or to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a valid s 8 notice to fence was given by you or to you
      `days since the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the notice was given
      `we agree on the need, the line and the kind of fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agree on all of: the need for the fence, where it goes, and what kind it is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the Magistrates Court about the new fence` IF
        `a notice to fence was given by me or to me`
    AND `days since the notice was given` GREATER THAN 21
    AND (NOT `we agree on the need, the line and the kind of fence`)

§§ `s 10 -- when my neighbour does not do their part`

-- s 10(1): where the owners agree, or the court has ordered under s 9, "and in either case either of those owners fails
-- within the time named in the agreement or order, or, if no time is named, within 3 months after the date of the
-- agreement or order, to perform his part ..., then the other of those owners may construct the whole fence as agreed
-- upon or determined by the order." (2): "The owner who constructs the fence ... may recover from the owner in default
-- half the cost thereof."
GIVEN `months named in the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the time allowed in months` MEANS
    IF `months named in the agreement or order` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `months named in the agreement or order`
    ELSE 3

@export May I build the whole fence myself and recover half the cost from my neighbour (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `we agreed the fence or the court ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agreed the fence after a notice to fence, or the court made an order under s 9
      `my neighbour has done their part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour has performed their part of the agreement or order
      `months named in the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER @desc The time the agreement or order gives to build, in months (0 if it names no time)
      `months since the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have passed since the date of the agreement or order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I build the whole fence and recover half` IF
        `we agreed the fence or the court ordered it`
    AND (NOT `my neighbour has done their part`)
    AND `months since the agreement or order` GREATER THAN `the time allowed in months` `months named in the agreement or order`

§§ `s 13 -- a fence built without a notice`

-- s 13(1): "When an owner of land has constructed a dividing fence that separates his land from adjoining land if the
-- fence is a sufficient fence, the owner of the adjoining land is liable to pay in accordance with the provisions of this
-- section half of the amount of the value of the fence."
-- (2): where the owner built it "without giving a notice pursuant to section 8" and has not received half its value,
-- "then if the adjoining owner -- (a) has completed ... the construction of any substantial building or structure on his
-- adjoining land; or (b) has occupied or occupies a building or structure constructed on the adjoining land; or (c) has
-- permitted or permits the lawful occupation by a person of a building or structure erected on the adjoining land, the
-- owner who constructed the fence may give to the owner of the adjoining land a notice claiming the payment of half of
-- the amount of the value of the fence as estimated at the date of the claim."
-- A fence built after a notice to fence is dealt with by ss 9-10; the encoding treats the s 13(2) claim as the route for
-- a fence built without one (encoder's reading of how ss 10 and 13 divide the ground).
DECLARE `My claim for a fence I built` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may give a notice claiming half the value as at the date of the claim (s 13(2))`
    `not yet: my neighbour has not built on, occupied or let a building on their land (s 13(2))`
    `no: the fence is not a sufficient fence (s 13(1))`
    `no: I have already received half the value`
    `not by s 13: I gave a notice to fence, so ss 9 and 10 apply`

@export Can I make my neighbour pay half the value of a fence I built without giving notice (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 13)?
GIVEN `the fence is a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence you built is a sufficient fence (s 5)
      `I gave a notice to fence before building` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a s 8 notice to fence before you built
      `my neighbour has built on, occupies or lets a building on their land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour has completed a substantial building or structure on their land, occupies one there, or lets someone lawfully occupy one
      `I have already received half the value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the land's previous owner) have already been paid half the value of the fence
GIVETH A `My claim for a fence I built`
DECIDE `Can I claim half the value of the fence I built` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `I gave a notice to fence before building` THEN `not by s 13: I gave a notice to fence, so ss 9 and 10 apply`
        IF NOT `the fence is a sufficient fence` THEN `no: the fence is not a sufficient fence (s 13(1))`
        IF `I have already received half the value` THEN `no: I have already received half the value`
        IF NOT `my neighbour has built on, occupies or lets a building on their land` THEN `not yet: my neighbour has not built on, occupied or let a building on their land (s 13(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I may give a notice claiming half the value as at the date of the claim (s 13(2))`

-- s 13(3): the adjoining owner who disputes the need, the desirability, the type or the value "may, within one month of
-- the receipt of the claim, give notice to the claimant owner that he disputes the claim." (4): in default of agreement
-- the builder may apply to the court. (7): if the adjoining owner does not "(a) pay the amount of the claim within one
-- month of the receipt by him thereof; or (b) within that period give notice ... that he disputes the claim ..., he is
-- liable to pay ... the amount of the claim."
DECLARE `Where I stand on a claim for half` IS ONE OF
    `I must pay the amount claimed: I neither paid nor disputed it within one month (s 13(7))`
    `the claim goes to the Magistrates Court if we cannot agree (s 13(4))`
    `settled: I have paid it`
    `not yet: I have one month from receiving the claim to pay it or dispute it in writing (s 13(3), (7))`

@export I have received a claim for half the value of a fence my neighbour built: must I pay it (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 13(3), (4), (7))?
GIVEN `I have paid it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the amount of the claim
      `I gave written notice disputing it within one month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within one month of receiving the claim, you gave written notice that you dispute it
      `a month has passed since I received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one month has passed since you received the claim
GIVETH A `Where I stand on a claim for half`
DECIDE `Must I pay my neighbour's claim for half` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `I have paid it` THEN `settled: I have paid it`
        IF `I gave written notice disputing it within one month` THEN `the claim goes to the Magistrates Court if we cannot agree (s 13(4))`
        IF `a month has passed since I received it` THEN `I must pay the amount claimed: I neither paid nor disputed it within one month (s 13(7))`
        OTHERWISE `not yet: I have one month from receiving the claim to pay it or dispute it in writing (s 13(3), (7))`

§§ `ss 14, 15 -- repairs`

-- s 14: "When a dividing fence is in need of repair the owners of land on either side of the fence are liable, subject to
-- the provisions of section 15, to join in or contribute in equal proportions to the repair of the fence." ("repair"
-- includes re-erect and realign, s 5.)
-- s 15(1): an owner "may give a notice to the owner of the adjoining land requiring him to assist in repairing the fence"
-- offering (2)(a) to repair it at both owners' cost in equal shares, (b) to let the other repair it at both owners' cost,
-- or (c) to bear half of a third party's repair, with a proposal of the kind and extent of repairs and the line.
-- (3): the owner given the notice "shall, within 14 days of the receipt by him of the notice, advise in writing" that he
-- (a) joins in one of the offered ways, (b) disputes the need, or (c) objects to the kind, extent or line.
-- (4): on (b) or (c) the owner who gave the notice "may apply to the court".
-- (7): if the owner given the notice fails to advise within 14 days, "the owner giving the notice may repair the fence
-- and demand and recover ... one-half of the cost of repairing the fence, but if -- (a) any dividing fence has been
-- constructed partly by one owner and partly by another owner each shall bear the cost of repairing the part so
-- constructed by him; (b) any dividing fence ... is damaged or destroyed by flood, fire, lightning, storm, tempest or
-- accident the owner of the land on either side of the fence may immediately repair it without any notice to the other
-- owner and is entitled to recover half of the expenses ...; (c) any dividing fence is damaged or destroyed ... by fire or
-- by the falling of any tree ... the owner of the land through whose neglect the fire originated ..., or the tree or part
-- thereof fell, is bound to repair or renew as soon as practicable".
-- (8): if the owner liable under (7)(c) fails to do so, "the owner of the adjoining land may repair or renew the fence and
-- recover from the owner so liable and in default the whole of the cost".
-- Fire appears in both (b) and (c). The encoding treats (c) as governing where the fire or the tree fall came through one
-- owner's neglect, and (b) where nobody's neglect caused it (encoder's reading). It reads "neglect" in (c) as qualifying
-- the tree as well as the fire.
DECLARE `How the fence came to need repair` IS ONE OF
    `wear, age or ordinary deterioration`
    `flood, fire, lightning, storm, tempest or accident, through nobody's neglect`
    `a fire or a falling tree through my neighbour's neglect`
    `a fire or a falling tree through my neglect`

DECLARE `Reply to my repair notice` IS ONE OF
    `no written reply`
    `agrees in writing to join in one of the ways I offered`
    `disputes the need or objects to the repairs, in writing`

DECLARE `What I can recover for a repair` IS ONE OF
    `half: I may repair at once without notice and recover half (s 15(7)(b))`
    `the whole: I may repair and recover the whole cost from my neighbour (s 15(8))`
    `nothing yet: my neighbour is bound to repair it as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    `nothing: I am bound to repair it myself as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    `half: my neighbour did not reply within 14 days, so I may repair and recover half (s 15(7))`
    `each of us bears the cost of repairing the part we built (s 15(7)(a))`
    `half, in the way my neighbour chose from my notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))`
    `the Magistrates Court decides: I may apply under s 15(4)`
    `nothing yet: I must give a repair notice and wait 14 days for a written reply (s 15(1), (3))`

@export What can I recover from my neighbour for repairing our dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair` @desc How the fence came to need repair
      `each of us built part of the fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence was built partly by you and partly by your neighbour
      `I gave a repair notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your neighbour a written s 15 notice requiring them to assist in repairing the fence
      `days since my neighbour received it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since your neighbour received the repair notice (0 if none given)
      `the reply` IS A `Reply to my repair notice` @desc What your neighbour replied in writing to your repair notice
      `my neighbour has failed to repair damage they are bound to repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the damage came from your neighbour's neglect: whether they have failed to repair or renew the fence
GIVETH A `What I can recover for a repair`
DECIDE `What can I recover for repairing the fence` IS
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `flood, fire, lightning, storm, tempest or accident, through nobody's neglect`
        THEN `half: I may repair at once without notice and recover half (s 15(7)(b))`
    WHEN `a fire or a falling tree through my neighbour's neglect`
        THEN IF `my neighbour has failed to repair damage they are bound to repair`
             THEN `the whole: I may repair and recover the whole cost from my neighbour (s 15(8))`
             ELSE `nothing yet: my neighbour is bound to repair it as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    WHEN `a fire or a falling tree through my neglect`
        THEN `nothing: I am bound to repair it myself as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    WHEN `wear, age or ordinary deterioration`
        THEN IF NOT `I gave a repair notice`
             THEN `nothing yet: I must give a repair notice and wait 14 days for a written reply (s 15(1), (3))`
             ELSE CONSIDER `the reply`
                  WHEN `agrees in writing to join in one of the ways I offered`
                      THEN `half, in the way my neighbour chose from my notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))`
                  WHEN `disputes the need or objects to the repairs, in writing`
                      THEN `the Magistrates Court decides: I may apply under s 15(4)`
                  WHEN `no written reply`
                      THEN IF `days since my neighbour received it` GREATER THAN 14
                           THEN IF `each of us built part of the fence`
                                THEN `each of us bears the cost of repairing the part we built (s 15(7)(a))`
                                ELSE `half: my neighbour did not reply within 14 days, so I may repair and recover half (s 15(7))`
                           ELSE `nothing yet: I must give a repair notice and wait 14 days for a written reply (s 15(1), (3))`

@export How much of the repair cost can I recover, given the answer to what I can recover (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `What I can recover for a repair` @desc The answer to "What can I recover for repairing the fence"
      `the cost of the repair` IS A NUMBER @desc What the repair cost, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the repair cost can I recover` IS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `half: I may repair at once without notice and recover half (s 15(7)(b))` THEN `the cost of the repair` DIVIDED BY 2
    WHEN `half: my neighbour did not reply within 14 days, so I may repair and recover half (s 15(7))` THEN `the cost of the repair` DIVIDED BY 2
    WHEN `half, in the way my neighbour chose from my notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))` THEN `the cost of the repair` DIVIDED BY 2
    WHEN `the whole: I may repair and recover the whole cost from my neighbour (s 15(8))` THEN `the cost of the repair`
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 19 -- landlord and tenant`

-- s 19(1): where a fence constructed or repaired under the Act divides land held by a tenant, the contribution as between
-- landlord and tenant, "unless otherwise agreed upon by the parties concerned", is payable: "(a) if the interest of the
-- tenant at the time of the construction or repair of the fence is less than for a term of 5 years, the landlord shall pay
-- the whole of the cost; (b) ... 5 years or more and less than ... 7 years, the landlord shall pay three-fourths ... and
-- the tenant ... one-fourth ...; (c) ... 7 years or more and less than ... 12 years, the landlord and the tenant shall
-- each pay one-half ...; (d) ... 12 years or more, the tenant shall pay the whole of the cost."
-- The table, as the tenant's fraction of the contribution, by the lower bound of the term in years.
DECLARE `Tenant band` HAS
    `term of at least` IS A NUMBER     -- years: the band starts at this term
    `tenant's fraction` IS A NUMBER    -- the part of the contribution the tenant bears

`the s 19 table` MEANS
    LIST (`Tenant band` OF 12, 1),
         (`Tenant band` OF 7, 0.5),
         (`Tenant band` OF 5, 0.25),
         (`Tenant band` OF 0, 0)

GIVEN `the term` IS A NUMBER
      `bands` IS A LIST OF `Tenant band`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first band reached` MEANS
    CONSIDER `bands`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN b FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `the term` AT LEAST b's `term of at least`
        THEN b's `tenant's fraction`
        ELSE `the first band reached` `the term` rest

@export As a tenant, what fraction of the contribution to a dividing fence must I bear as against my landlord, absent an agreement (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `the term of my lease in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The term of your tenancy, in years, at the time the fence is built or repaired
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fraction of the fence cost do I bear as tenant` IS
    `the first band reached` `the term of my lease in years` `the s 19 table`

§§ `s 21 -- entering the neighbour's land`

-- s 21: "Every person engaged in constructing or repairing a fence under this Act and his agents and servants may, at all
-- reasonable times during the construction or repairing, enter upon the lands adjoining the fence and do upon those lands
-- such acts, matters and things as are necessary or reasonably required to carry into effect the construction or
-- repairing of the fence."
@export May I go onto my neighbour's land to build or repair the dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `I am building or repairing the fence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your agent or contractor) are constructing or repairing the fence under the Act
      `it is a reasonable time during the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a reasonable time during the construction or repair
      `what I do there is necessary or reasonably required for the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you would do on the land is necessary or reasonably required to build or repair the fence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I enter my neighbour's land for the fence work` IF
        `I am building or repairing the fence under the Act`
    AND `it is a reasonable time during the work`
    AND `what I do there is necessary or reasonably required for the work`
